{"audio": "1timothy-03.opus", "duration_ms": 124348, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 3820, "text": "1 Timothy, Chapter Three."}, {"start_ms": 5080, "end_ms": 10981, "text": "This is a trustworthy saying: If anyone aspires to be an overseer, he desires a noble task."}, {"start_ms": 11641, "end_ms": 26802, "text": "An overseer, then, must be above reproach, the husband of but one wife, temperate, self-controlled, respectable, hospitable, able to teach, not dependent on wine, not violent but gentle, peaceable, and free of the love of money."}, {"start_ms": 27802, "end_ms": 33722, "text": "An overseer must manage his own household well and keep his children under control, with complete dignity."}, {"start_ms": 34582, "end_ms": 39843, "text": "For if someone does not know how to manage his own household, how can he care for the church of God?"}, {"start_ms": 40523, "end_ms": 46383, "text": "He must not be a recent convert, or he may become conceited and fall under the same condemnation as the devil."}, {"start_ms": 47343, "end_ms": 53743, "text": "Furthermore, he must have a good reputation with outsiders, so that he will not fall into disgrace and into the snare of the devil."}, {"start_ms": 54964, "end_ms": 60684, "text": "Deacons likewise must be dignified, not double-tongued or given to much wine or greedy for money."}, {"start_ms": 61104, "end_ms": 64164, "text": "They must hold to the mystery of the faith with a clear conscience."}, {"start_ms": 64684, "end_ms": 67004, "text": "Additionally, they must first be tested."}, {"start_ms": 67444, "end_ms": 71025, "text": "Then, if they are above reproach, let them serve as deacons."}, {"start_ms": 71965, "end_ms": 77585, "text": "In the same way, the women must be dignified, not slanderers, but temperate and faithful in all things."}, {"start_ms": 78145, "end_ms": 83605, "text": "A deacon must be the husband of but one wife, a good manager of his children and of his own household."}, {"start_ms": 84405, "end_ms": 92086, "text": "For those who have served well as deacons acquire for themselves a high standing and great confidence in the faith that is in Christ Jesus."}, {"start_ms": 93466, "end_ms": 106827, "text": "Although I hope to come to you soon, I am writing you these things in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in God’s household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth."}, {"start_ms": 107847, "end_ms": 122688, "text": "By common confession, the mystery of godliness is great: He appeared in the flesh, was vindicated by the Spirit, was seen by angels, was proclaimed among the nations, was believed in throughout the world, was taken up in glory."}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 2440, "si": 0}, {"t": "Timothy,", "s": 2440, "e": 2800, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 3160, "e": 3500, "si": 0}, {"t": "Three.", "s": 3560, "e": 3820, "si": 0}, {"t": "This", "s": 5080, "e": 5300, "si": 1}, {"t": "is", "s": 5460, "e": 5580, "si": 1}, {"t": "a", "s": 5660, "e": 5680, "si": 1}, {"t": "trustworthy", "s": 5840, "e": 6360, "si": 1}, {"t": "saying:", "s": 6480, "e": 6780, "si": 1}, {"t": "If", "s": 7220, "e": 7300, "si": 1}, {"t": "anyone", "s": 7380, "e": 7760, "si": 1}, {"t": "aspires", "s": 7781, "e": 8321, "si": 1}, {"t": "to", "s": 8381, "e": 8461, "si": 1}, {"t": "be", "s": 8481, "e": 8541, "si": 1}, {"t": "an", "s": 8601, "e": 8681, "si": 1}, {"t": "overseer,", "s": 8741, "e": 9281, "si": 1}, {"t": "he", "s": 9381, "e": 9461, "si": 1}, {"t": "desires", "s": 9561, "e": 10101, "si": 1}, {"t": "a", "s": 10141, "e": 10161, "si": 1}, {"t": "noble", "s": 10241, "e": 10541, "si": 1}, {"t": "task.", "s": 10581, "e": 10981, "si": 1}, {"t": "An", "s": 11641, "e": 11701, "si": 2}, {"t": "overseer,", "s": 11801, "e": 12301, "si": 2}, {"t": "then,", "s": 12361, "e": 12581, "si": 2}, {"t": "must", "s": 12721, "e": 12941, "si": 2}, {"t": "be", "s": 12981, "e": 13041, "si": 2}, {"t": "above", "s": 13141, "e":